  "commands_note": "A Bash or PowerShell allow rule gives the caps of every entry it matches (unioned). Words are matched after wrappers (sudo -u x, env A=b, timeout 30, nice -n 5, xargs...) and leading NAME=value assignments are skipped. match 'any': a wildcard rule for the command. match 'verbs': the rule names one of the verbs (with 'wildcard': true, only a wildcard rule ending right after the verb, like `npm run:*`); a bare wildcard for the command gives 'bare_caps'; 'read_verbs' add 'read_caps'; with 'groups': true a wildcard after one subcommand (`gh pr:*`, `aws s3:*`) counts as bare. match 'bare': a wildcard rule for the interpreter itself, or for one of its run-this-code flags. Commands not listed here are not classified: names only.",
